--- a/README
+++ b/README
@@ -22,11 +22,33 @@
 either through curl-config or the internal list of guesses, you can specify
 an explicit path when building the Makefile:
 
-    perl Makefile.PL /home/foo/curl/include
+    perl Makefile.PL /opt/curl/include
 
 If you want to specify which curl-config to use instead of the first in path 
 set the environment variable CURL_CONFIG to point at the curl-config to use.
 
+If curl-config omits a system include directory, Makefile.PL asks Perl's
+configured compiler to locate curl/curl.h. It uses the same compiler and
+curl-config flags to extract constants. Function macros and empty header
+guards are excluded from the generated integer constants.
+
+The XS code accepts both old and current libcurl multi header guards and
+uses libcurl's public handle typedefs. These changes apply to ordinary Perl
+and XPerl without depending on the interpreter's numeric or thread settings.
+
+The local regression tests need no network access:
+
+    make test TEST_FILES='t/00constants.t t/20undefined_subs.t t/22local.t'
+
+Cookie tests load a temporary Netscape cookie file and check the returned
+entry. They do not require a public website to set cookies. The full test
+suite still includes network transfers. CURL_TEST_URL selects an alternative
+HTTP test URL, which need not set cookies.
+
+When porting tests, use local fixtures for data whose contents matter.
+Keep generic libcurl fixes available to ordinary Perl. Use XPERL_VERSION
+for conditional XS code only when an XPerl API difference requires it.
+
 Minimum version requirements:
 
 This module, starting from version 4 requires at least Perl 5.6.1 and libcurl 7.10.8.
